# Game logic

## Units and space
- 1 world unit = 1 m; `CONFIG.planetR` = 80. Surface motion = geodesic (`slerpDirection` / `stepToward`), not Euclidean chord length as “walk distance”.
- Directions on the planet = normalized `dir` from the center; height = `terrain.height(dir)` / `sampleSurface`.
- Water: `wetness` (ocean flood), not merely `length() < waterLevel`.

## Terrain
- One geometry = pick, morph, shadows, colors, FOW attributes.
- Morph API (`elevate`/`depress`/driven) — do not rewrite vertex positions outside the existing morph queue.
- After morph, rely on `updateMorphs` + partial normals; shore/trees refresh via existing dirty paths in `main`.

## Spells
- Data in `SPELLS` (`defs.js`); runtime in `SpellSystem` + the spell file.
- Wizard damage: respect `dead`, `remote`, `godMode`, `immortal` (see patterns in comet/volcano/earthquake).
- Local cast vs MP: `castAs(wizard, …)` must work for a remote owner without double damage on the host (`cast` intent runs FX+morph on every client).

## Animals / blockers
- Host simulates herds; remotes receive `world` / `beast` intents (`net/intents.js`, `world-sync.js`).
- `markHerdRemote` — do not run authoritative AI on the client.
- Movement collision via `Blockers`, not a custom brute-force loop when the API is enough.

## Tunables
- New gameplay number → `CONFIG` or `SPELLS[id]`, with a short JSDoc comment matching nearby keys (Czech comments in code are fine / keep consistency with neighbors).
